<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include several appendices with additional details, derivations, and results.
Our framework allows general SDEs with matrix-valued diffusion coefficients that depend on the state, for which we provide a detailed discussion in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>. We give a full derivation of VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, and discuss how to use them from a practitioner’s perspective in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C SDEs in the wild ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. We elaborate on the probability flow formulation of our framework in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, including a derivation of the probability flow ODE (<a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Derivation ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>), exact likelihood computation (<a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Likelihood computation ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>), probability flow sampling with a fixed discretization strategy (<a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Probability flow sampling ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>), sampling with black-box ODE solvers (<a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Sampling with black-box ODE solvers ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>), and experimental verification on uniquely identifiable encoding (<a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Uniquely identifiable encoding ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>). We give a full description of the reverse diffusion sampler in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Reverse diffusion sampling ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, the DDPM-type ancestral sampler for SMLD models in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Ancestral sampling for SMLD models ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, and Predictor-Corrector samplers in <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Predictor-Corrector samplers ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>. We explain our model architectures and detailed experimental settings in <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Architecture improvements ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>, with <math id="Ax1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024\times 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024\times 1024</annotation></semantics></math> CelebA-HQ samples therein. Finally, we detail on the algorithms for controllable generation in <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>, and include extended results for class-conditional generation (<a href="#A9.SS1" title="I.1 Class-conditional sampling ‣ Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.1</span></a>), image inpainting (<a href="#A9.SS2" title="I.2 Imputation ‣ Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.2</span></a>), colorization (<a href="#A9.SS3" title="I.3 Colorization ‣ Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a>), and a strategy for solving general inverse problems (<a href="#A9.SS4" title="I.4 Solving general inverse problems ‣ Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The framework for more general SDEs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text, we introduced our framework based on a simplified SDE <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.1 Perturbing data with SDEs ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> where the diffusion coefficient is independent of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. It turns out that our framework can be extended to hold for more general diffusion coefficients. We can consider SDEs in the following form:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We follow the Itô interpretation of SDEs throughout this paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson, 1982</a>)</cite>, the reverse-time SDE is given by (<em id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cf</em>.<span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2 Generating samples by reversing the SDE ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\}\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\}\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we define <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}):=(\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{1}(\mathbf{x}),\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{2}(\mathbf{x}),\cdots,\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{d}(\mathbf{x}))^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}):=(\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{1}(\mathbf{x}),\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{2}(\mathbf{x}),\cdots,\nabla\cdot\mathbf{f}^{d}(\mathbf{x}))^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> for a matrix-valued function <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}):=(\mathbf{f}^{1}(\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{f}^{2}(\mathbf{x}),\cdots,\mathbf{f}^{d}(\mathbf{x}))^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐟</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}):=(\mathbf{f}^{1}(\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{f}^{2}(\mathbf{x}),\cdots,\mathbf{f}^{d}(\mathbf{x}))^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The probability flow ODE corresponding to <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> has the following form (<em id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cf</em>.<span id="A1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, <a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.3 Probability flow and connection to neural ODEs ‣ 4 Solving the reverse SDE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, see a detailed derivation in <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Derivation ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\bigg\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\frac{1}{2}\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\bigg\}\mathrm{d}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\bigg\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\frac{1}{2}\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\bigg\}\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Finally for conditional generation with the general SDE <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we can solve the conditional reverse-time SDE below (<em id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cf</em>.<span id="A1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, <a href="#S5.E14" title="In 5 Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, details in <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Controllable generation ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\\
-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\}\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\{\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)-\nabla\cdot[\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}]-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\\
-\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\}\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When the drift and diffusion coefficient of an SDE are not affine, it can be difficult to compute the transition kernel <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math> in closed form. This hinders the training of score-based models, because <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Estimating scores for the SDE ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> requires knowing <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\log p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\log p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math>. To overcome this difficulty, we can replace denoising score matching in <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Estimating scores for the SDE ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with other efficient variants of score matching that do not require computing <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\log p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\log p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, when using sliced score matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2019a</a>)</cite>, our training objective <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Estimating scores for the SDE ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> becomes</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}=\argmin_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{t}\bigg\{\lambda(t)\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}(0)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{v}\sim p_{\mathbf{v}}}\bigg[\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}(t),t)\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\mathbf{v}^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}(t),t)\mathbf{v}\bigg]\bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}=\argmin_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{t}\bigg\{\lambda(t)\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}(0)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}(t)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{v}\sim p_{\mathbf{v}}}\bigg[\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}(t),t)\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\mathbf{v}^{\mkern-1.5mu\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}(t),t)\mathbf{v}\bigg]\bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:[0,T]\to\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:[0,T]\to\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive weighting function, <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{v}]=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{v}]=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{v}]=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{v}]=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can always simulate the SDE to sample from <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math>, and solve <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> to train the time-dependent score-based model <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide detailed derivations to show that the noise perturbations of SMLD and DDPM are discretizations of the Variance Exploding (VE) and Variance Preserving (VP) SDEs respectively. We additionally introduce sub-VP SDEs, a modification to VP SDEs that often achieves better performance in both sample quality and likelihoods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, when using a total of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> noise scales, each perturbation kernel <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{i}}(\mathbf{x}\mid\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{i}}(\mathbf{x}\mid\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> of SMLD can be derived from the following Markov chain:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}\sim p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have introduced <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify the notation.
In the limit of <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the Markov chain <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a continuous stochastic process <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a function <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, where we have used a continuous time variable <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for indexing, rather than an integer <math id="A2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,\cdots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,\cdots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\cdots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\cdots,N</annotation></semantics></math>. We can rewrite <a href="#A2.E20" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> as follows with <math id="A2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\big\{0,\frac{1}{N},\cdots,\frac{N-1}{N}\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\big\{0,\frac{1}{N},\cdots,\frac{N-1}{N}\big\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}(t+\Delta t)=\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(t+\Delta t)-\sigma^{2}(t)}~\mathbf{z}(t)\approx\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\left[\sigma^{2}(t)\right]}{\mathrm{d}t}\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}(t+\Delta t)=\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(t+\Delta t)-\sigma^{2}(t)}~\mathbf{z}(t)\approx\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\left[\sigma^{2}(t)\right]}{\mathrm{d}t}\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the approximate equality holds when <math id="A2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the limit of <math id="A2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, this converges to</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\left[\sigma^{2}(t)\right]}{\mathrm{d}t}}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\left[\sigma^{2}(t)\right]}{\mathrm{d}t}}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which is the VE SDE.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the perturbation kernels <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{\alpha_{i}}(\mathbf{x}\mid\mathbf{x}_{0})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{\alpha_{i}}(\mathbf{x}\mid\mathbf{x}_{0})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> used in DDPM, the discrete Markov chain is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\sqrt{1-\beta_{i}}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\beta_{i}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\sqrt{1-\beta_{i}}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\beta_{i}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>. To obtain the limit of this Markov chain when <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we define an auxiliary set of noise scales <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\bar{\beta}_{i}=N\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\beta}_{i}=N\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and re-write <a href="#A2.E22" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> as below</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\sqrt{1-\frac{\bar{\beta}_{i}}{N}}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\frac{\bar{\beta}_{i}}{N}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{i}=\sqrt{1-\frac{\bar{\beta}_{i}}{N}}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\sqrt{\frac{\bar{\beta}_{i}}{N}}\mathbf{z}_{i-1},\quad i=1,\cdots,N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In the limit of <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\beta}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\beta}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a function <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\bar{\beta}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\left(\frac{i}{N}\right)=\bar{\beta}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(\frac{i}{N})=\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(\frac{i}{N})=\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(\frac{i}{N})=\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(\frac{i}{N})=\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can rewrite the Markov chain <a href="#A2.E23" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> as the following with <math id="A2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,1,\cdots,\frac{N-1}{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,1,\cdots,\frac{N-1}{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}(t+\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}(t+\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{1-\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{1-\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{x}(t)-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{x}(t)-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t+\Delta t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{x}(t)-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\Delta t~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{x}(t)-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\Delta t~\mathbf{x}(t)+\sqrt{\beta(t)\Delta t}~\mathbf{z}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where the approximate equality holds when <math id="A2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, in the limit of <math id="A2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A2.E24" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> converges to the following VP SDE:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}~\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\beta(t)}~\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}~\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\beta(t)}~\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">So far, we have demonstrated that the noise perturbations used in SMLD and DDPM correspond to discretizations of VE and VP SDEs respectively. The VE SDE always yields a process with exploding variance when <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, the VP SDE yields a process with bounded variance. In addition, the process has a constant unit variance for all <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math> has a unit variance. Since the VP SDE has affine drift and diffusion coefficients, we can use Eq. (5.51) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Särkkä &amp; Solin (2019)</a></cite> to obtain an ODE that governs the evolution of variance</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\beta(t)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\beta(t)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)\coloneqq\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{x}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)\coloneqq\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{x}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> obeying a VP SDE. Solving this ODE, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}+e^{\int_{0}^{t}-\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)-\mathbf{I})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}+e^{\int_{0}^{t}-\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)-\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">from which it is clear that the variance <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is always bounded given <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)\equiv\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)\equiv\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to this difference, we name <a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.4 Examples: VE, VP SDEs and beyond ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> as the <em id="A2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Variance Exploding (VE) SDE</em>, and <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.4 Examples: VE, VP SDEs and beyond ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> the <em id="A2.p4.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Variance Preserving (VP) SDE</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Inspired by the VP SDE, we propose a new SDE called the <em id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sub-VP SDE</em>, namely</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}~\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\beta(t)(1-e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)\mathbf{x}~\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\beta(t)(1-e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Following standard derivations, it is straightforward to show that <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math> is the same for both VP and sub-VP SDEs; the variance function of sub-VP SDEs is different, given by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}+e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}\mathbf{I}+e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(0)-2\mathbf{I})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}+e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}\mathbf{I}+e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(0)-2\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)\coloneqq\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{x}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)\coloneqq\operatorname{Cov}[\mathbf{x}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math> for a process <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}(t)\}_{t=0}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by solving <a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>. In addition, we observe that (i) <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)\preccurlyeq\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)\preccurlyeq\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(0)=\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(0)=\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and shared <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(s)</annotation></semantics></math>; and (ii) <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)=\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>sub-VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mtext>VP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{sub-VP}}(t)=\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{\text{VP}}(t)=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The former is why we name <a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> the sub-VP SDE—its variance is always upper bounded by the corresponding VP SDE. The latter justifies the use of sub-VP SDEs for score-based generative modeling, since they can perturb any data distribution to standard Gaussian under suitable conditions, just like VP SDEs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs all have affine drift coefficients. Therefore, their perturbation kernels <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))</annotation></semantics></math> are all Gaussian and can be computed with Eqs. (5.50) and (5.51) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Särkkä &amp; Solin (2019)</a></cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))=\begin{cases}\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0),[\sigma^{2}(t)-\sigma^{2}(0)]\mathbf{I}\big),&amp;~~~\text{(VE SDE)}\\
\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0)e^{-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s},\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{I}e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}\big)&amp;~~~\text{(VP SDE)}\\
\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0)e^{-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s},[1-e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}]^{2}\mathbf{I}\big)&amp;~~~\text{(sub-VP SDE)}\end{cases}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>(VE SDE)</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>(VP SDE)</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>(sub-VP SDE)</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))=\begin{cases}\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0),[\sigma^{2}(t)-\sigma^{2}(0)]\mathbf{I}\big),&amp;~~~\text{(VE SDE)}\\
\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0)e^{-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s},\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{I}e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}\big)&amp;~~~\text{(VP SDE)}\\
\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0)e^{-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s},[1-e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)\mathrm{d}s}]^{2}\mathbf{I}\big)&amp;~~~\text{(sub-VP SDE)}\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">As a result, all SDEs introduced here can be efficiently trained with the objective in <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Estimating scores for the SDE ‣ 3 Score-based generative modeling with SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>SDEs in the wild</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we discuss concrete instantiations of VE and VP SDEs whose discretizations yield SMLD and DDPM models, and the specific sub-VP SDE used in our experiments. In SMLD, the noise scales <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically a geometric sequence where <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed to <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen according to Technique 1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song &amp; Ermon (2020)</a></cite>. Usually, SMLD models normalize image inputs to the range <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric sequence, we have <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\frac{i}{N})=\sigma_{i}=\sigma_{\text{min}}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\right)^{\frac{i-1}{N-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\frac{i}{N})=\sigma_{i}=\sigma_{\text{min}}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\right)^{\frac{i-1}{N-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\cdots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\cdots,N</annotation></semantics></math>. In the limit of <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{min}}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\right)^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{min}}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\right)^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding VE SDE is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sigma_{\text{min}}\bigg(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\bigg)^{t}\sqrt{2\log\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in(0,1]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sigma_{\text{min}}\bigg(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\bigg)^{t}\sqrt{2\log\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in(0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the perturbation kernel can be derived via <a href="#A2.E29" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0),\sigma_{\text{min}}^{2}\Big(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\Big)^{2t}\mathbf{I}\right),\quad t\in(0,1]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);\mathbf{x}(0),\sigma_{\text{min}}^{2}\Big(\frac{\sigma_{\text{max}}}{\sigma_{\text{min}}}\Big)^{2t}\mathbf{I}\right),\quad t\in(0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">There is one subtlety when <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>: by definition, <math id="A3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(0)=\sigma_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(0)=\sigma_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> (following the convention in <a href="#A2.E20" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), but <math id="A3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(0^{+})\coloneqq\lim_{t\to 0^{+}}\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{min}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(0^{+})\coloneqq\lim_{t\to 0^{+}}\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{min}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="A3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for SMLD is not differentiable since <math id="A3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(0)\neq\sigma(0^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(0)\neq\sigma(0^{+})</annotation></semantics></math>, causing the VE SDE in <a href="#A2.E21" title="In Appendix B VE, VP and sub-VP SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> undefined for <math id="A3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, we bypass this issue by always solving the SDE and its associated probability flow ODE in the range <math id="A3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[\epsilon,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[\epsilon,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for some small constant <math id="A3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use <math id="A3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> in our VE SDE experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For DDPM models, <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically an arithmetic sequence where <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}=\frac{\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}{N}+\frac{i-1}{N(N-1)}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}=\frac{\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}{N}+\frac{i-1}{N(N-1)}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\cdots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\cdots,N</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)=\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)=\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> in the limit of <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. This corresponds to the following instantiation of the VP SDE:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}))\mathbf{x}\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in[0,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=-\frac{1}{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}))\mathbf{x}\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}+t(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})}\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in[0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(0)\sim p_{\text{data}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(0)\sim p_{\text{data}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. In our experiments, we let <math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}=20</annotation></semantics></math> to match the settings in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al. (2020)</a></cite>. The perturbation kernel is given by</p>
<table id="A3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))\\
=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);e^{-\frac{1}{4}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-\frac{1}{2}t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\mathbf{x}(0),\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{I}e^{-\frac{1}{2}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\right),\quad t\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))\\
=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);e^{-\frac{1}{4}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-\frac{1}{2}t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\mathbf{x}(0),\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{I}e^{-\frac{1}{2}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\right),\quad t\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For DDPM, there is no discontinuity issue with the corresponding VP SDE; yet, there are numerical instability issues for training and sampling at <math id="A3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, due to the vanishing variance of <math id="A3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, same as the VE SDE, we restrict computation to <math id="A3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[\epsilon,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[\epsilon,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for a small <math id="A3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For sampling, we choose <math id="A3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> so that the variance of <math id="A3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> in VP SDE matches the variance of <math id="A3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in DDPM; for training and likelihood computation, we adopt <math id="A3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> which empirically gives better results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A3.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2011.13456v2/NCSN_var.svg" id="A3.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/412;" width="548" height="412"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>SMLD</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A3.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2011.13456v2/ddpm_mean.svg" id="A3.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/428;" width="548" height="428"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>DDPM (mean)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A3.F5.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2011.13456v2/ddpm_var.svg" id="A3.F5.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/428;" width="548" height="428"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>DDPM (variance)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Discrete-time perturbation kernels and our continuous generalizations match each other almost exactly. (a) compares the variance of perturbation kernels for SMLD and VE SDE; (b) compares the scaling factors of means of perturbation kernels for DDPM and VP SDE; and (c) compares the variance of perturbation kernels for DDPM and VP SDE.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As a sanity check for our SDE generalizations to SMLD and DDPM, we compare the perturbation kernels of SDEs and original discrete Markov chains in <a href="#A3.F5" title="In Appendix C SDEs in the wild ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. The SMLD and DDPM models both use <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1000</annotation></semantics></math> noise scales. For SMLD, we only need to compare the variances of perturbation kernels since means are the same by definition. For DDPM, we compare the scaling factors of means and the variances. As demonstrated in <a href="#A3.F5" title="In Appendix C SDEs in the wild ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the discrete perturbation kernels of original SMLD and DDPM models align well with perturbation kernels derived from VE and VP SDEs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For sub-VP SDEs, we use exactly the same <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as VP SDEs. This leads to the following perturbation kernel</p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))\\
=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);e^{-\frac{1}{4}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-\frac{1}{2}t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\mathbf{x}(0),[1-e^{-\frac{1}{2}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}]^{2}\mathbf{I}\right),\quad t\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0t}(\mathbf{x}(t)\mid\mathbf{x}(0))\\
=\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t);e^{-\frac{1}{4}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-\frac{1}{2}t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}\mathbf{x}(0),[1-e^{-\frac{1}{2}t^{2}(\bar{\beta}_{\text{max}}-\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}})-t\bar{\beta}_{\text{min}}}]^{2}\mathbf{I}\right),\quad t\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We also restrict numerical computation to the same interval of <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\epsilon,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\epsilon,1]</annotation></semantics></math> as VP SDEs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Empirically, we observe that smaller <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> generally yields better likelihood values for all SDEs. For sampling, it is important to use an appropriate <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for better Inception scores and FIDs, although samples across different <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> look visually the same to human eyes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Probability flow ODE</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Derivation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The idea of probability flow ODE is inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maoutsa et al. (2020)</a></cite>, and one can find the derivation of a simplified case therein. Below we provide a derivation for the fully general ODE in <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>. We consider the SDE in <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Appendix A The framework for more general SDEs ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, which possesses the following form:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x},t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}(\cdot,t):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The marginal probability density <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\mathbf{x}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\mathbf{x}(t))</annotation></semantics></math> evolves according to Kolmogorov’s forward equation (Fokker-Planck equation) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Øksendal, 2003</a>)</cite></p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial t}=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{i}\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial t}=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{i}\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We can easily rewrite <a href="#A4.E35" title="In D.1 Derivation ‣ Appendix D Probability flow ODE ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> to obtain</p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial p_{t}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{i}\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{i}\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big]\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}[f_{i}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\Big[\sum_{k=1}^{d}G_{ik}(\mathbf{x},t)G_{jk}(\mathbf{x},t)p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\Big]\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
