</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The corrector algorithms</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We take the schedule of annealed Langevin dynamics in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song &amp; Ermon (2019)</a></cite>, but re-frame it with slight modifications in order to get better interpretability and empirical performance. We provide the corrector algorithms in <a href="#alg4" title="In The corrector algorithms ‣ Appendix G Predictor-Corrector samplers ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithms</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#alg5" title="Algorithm 5 ‣ The corrector algorithms ‣ Appendix G Predictor-Corrector samplers ‣ Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> respectively, where we call <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> the “signal-to-noise” ratio. We determine the step size <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> using the norm of the Gaussian noise <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, norm of the score-based model <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{s}_{{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}}\right\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{s}_{{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}}\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the signal-to-noise ratio <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. When sampling a large batch of samples together, we replace the norm <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with the average norm across the mini-batch. When the batch size is small, we suggest replacing <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the dimensionality of <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_top ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:194.8pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> Corrector algorithm (VE SDE).</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},r,N,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},r,N,M</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{N}^{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{\text{max}}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{N}^{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{\text{max}}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow N</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg4.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}\leftarrow\mathbf{s}_{{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j-1},\sigma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}\leftarrow\mathbf{s}_{{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{*}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j-1},\sigma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leftarrow 2(r\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}/\left\lVert\mathbf{g}\right\rVert_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leftarrow 2(r\left\lVert\mathbf{z}\right\rVert_{2}/\left\lVert\mathbf{g}\right\rVert_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg4.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j-1}+\epsilon~\mathbf{g}+\sqrt{2\epsilon}~\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{j-1}+\epsilon~\mathbf{g}+\sqrt{2\epsilon}~\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg4.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg4.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i-1}^{0}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i-1}^{0}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg4.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
